{# Ward template: .github/copilot-instructions.md for operations/GitOps repositories #}
When reviewing changes in this GitOps operations repository, focus on the following areas:

## YAML & Helm
- Validate YAML syntax and indentation (2-space indent, no tabs)
- Check Helm `values.yaml` structure: all required fields present (image, resources, probes, service, ingress)
- Verify `Chart.yaml`: `appVersion` and chart `version` are set correctly
- Flag any hardcoded image tags that should use `latest` or semantic versions
- Ensure Helm template values are properly quoted when needed
- Verify `imagePullPolicy: Always` when using `latest` tags

## Secrets & Security
- No plaintext secrets, passwords, tokens, or credentials anywhere in the repo
- Secrets must use SealedSecrets or external secret management (e.g., Azure KeyVault, AWS Secrets Manager)
- Flag any base64-encoded values that look like credentials but aren't SealedSecrets
- No sensitive data in ConfigMaps — use Secrets or external vaults instead
- No wildcard RBAC permissions unless explicitly justified

## Configuration Consistency
- Verify test and production configs are structurally consistent
- Flag settings present in test but missing in production (or vice versa)
- No environment-specific values in base config — only in profile-specific files
- Verify no duplicate property keys within the same YAML file

## Resource & Probe Configuration
- Resource requests and limits must be set for all containers
- Production resource limits should be >= test limits
- Liveness and readiness probes must be configured
- `initialDelaySeconds` should be sufficient for application startup
- Verify memory settings (`-Xms`, `-Xmx`) fit within container memory limits

## Deployment Safety
- Pod disruption budgets should exist for production services (`minAvailable: "1"`)
- Replica counts: production should have >= 2 replicas
- Auto-rollout annotations must not be removed without justification
